s governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'geophysical methods; Core considerations include the defining characteristics of geophysical methods, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it; Engineering Geology', 'Active'), ('KCR_000459', 'landslides', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Engineering Geology', 'Technical Concept', 'Rapid or slow downslope movements of soil, rock, or debris along a failure surface.', 'Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of landslides within Engineering Geology, particularly where the Geological Hazards module establishes its technical context.', 'Core considerations include the defining characteristics of landslides, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'Rapid or slow downslope movements of soil, rock, or debris along a failure surface. Within Geological Hazards, the concept covers Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of landslides within Engineering Geology, particularly where the Geological Hazards module establishes its technical context. Key technical considerations are Core considerations include the defining characteristics of landslides, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'landslides; Core considerations include the defining characteristics of landslides, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it; Engineering Geology', 'Active'), ('KCR_000460', 'earthquakes', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Engineering Geology', 'Technical Concept', 'Sudden release of stored geological strain that generates seismic waves and ground motion