is, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of subsidence within Engineering Geology, particularly where the Geological Hazards module establishes its technical context. Key technical considerations are Core considerations include the defining characteristics of subsidence, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'subsidence; Core considerations include the defining characteristics of subsidence, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it; Engineering Geology', 'Active'), ('KCR_000462', 'expansive materials', 'Engineering & Technology', 'Engineering Geology', 'Technical Concept', 'Soils or rocks that undergo significant volume change, particularly swelling and shrinkage, when their moisture state changes.', 'Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of expansive materials within Engineering Geology, particularly where the Geological Hazards module establishes its technical context.', 'Core considerations include the defining characteristics of expansive materials, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'Soils or rocks that undergo significant volume change, particularly swelling and shrinkage, when their moisture state changes. Within Geological Hazards, the concept covers Applies to the analysis, design, implementation, interpretation, or evaluation of expansive materials within Engineering Geology, particularly where the Geological Hazards module establishes its technical context. Key technical considerations are Core considerations include the defining characteristics of expansive materials, its governing relationships or mechanisms, applicable assumptions and constraints, and criteria used to analyse or evaluate it.', 'expansive materials; Core conside